  because the older bundled SQLite 3.39.4 rejects Tool Shed accounting-trigger JSON functions with
  `trusted_schema=OFF`. The project added a manual instruction and dashboard-scheduler interpreter
  pin. Doctor still reported `HEALTHY` under the read-capable 3.11.2 runtime, revealing that current
  health checks do not prove mutation compatibility.
- The final checkpoint retained `INV-0001` with a resolvable `Parent:` path to `MAP-0001`, while the
  database relationship table remained empty and `document_store related/context` returned no
  relationship. Byte/render parity therefore did not establish relationship parity.
- The convergence also applied a readiness review and historical outcome backfill. These may have
  been intentional in that run, but they demonstrate why schema conversion, required semantic
  migration, and optional semantic enrichment must be separately inventoried and authorized.
- No implementation, migration, cutover, release, or publication is authorized by this
  brainstorming route.

